I doubt the version I have is the "official" one, so maybe this is only
directed to whoever put the copy up at atari.archive.umich.edu.

Anyway, when you die or quit and hit "q" instead of looking at your inventory
and intrinsics, this version does not just dump back to whatever shell you
were using.  Instead it turns off the text and displays the hi-score list.
I can tell it's displaying the hi-score list because the cursor scans down
a little bit and rests about 1/3 the way down.  Then it indents, right
where it is trying to say "Hit RETURN", sits there, and blinks on and off.

By "turns off the text" I mean it makes the text the same color as the
background screencolor, thereby making it invisible.  The problem is that
it's never turned back into a color.  So when I get dumped back into
my Gulam shell I can't see anything.  

Hopefully this can be avoided in the offical release.


